{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GsgCDMkiXoDWxhFWaDooUi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Conference on Robot Learning (@corl_conf) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/corl_conf?lang=en\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific details about a dedicated reviewer guidelines page with a review form for 2026 were not prominently displayed in the results. However, here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Key Information:\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and submissions are being managed through OpenReview.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements:\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Guidance:\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines were not returned in the search, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines provide insights into the review process. Reviewers are encouraged to be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful, start with the positive aspects, and suggest improvements.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend visiting the official CoRL website at corl.org or checking the OpenReview platform directly, as these resources may have more comprehensive documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"5d79e193-eb89-489f-8d65-fcd5139cd3bd","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:05:24.226Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HhUxzc9tNCGePFYjDHUvng","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Conference on Robot Learning (@corl_conf) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/corl_conf?lang=en"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific details about a dedicated reviewer guidelines page with a review form for 2026 were not prominently displayed in the results. However, here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Key Information:\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US, and submissions are being managed through OpenReview.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements:\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n## Review Guidance:\n\nWhile specific 2026 reviewer guidelines were not returned in the search, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines provide insights into the review process. Reviewers are encouraged to be constructive and concrete; be courteous and respectful, start with the positive aspects, and suggest improvements.\n\nFor the most current and detailed CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend visiting the official CoRL website at corl.org or checking the OpenReview platform directly, as these resources may have more comprehensive documentation."],"durationSeconds":6.172473827999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Ty3yNsWqwXoGZXA6eEEph","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review criteria scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FDemos\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found some information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, though the most detailed results I found are from CoRL 2023 and CoRL 2024.\n\nFor **CoRL 2024**, submissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor **CoRL 2023**, the reviewer guidelines included the following key points:\n\n- CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation\n- Obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores\n- Reviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, and start with the positive aspects before suggesting improvements\n\nThe search results indicate that the OpenReview page for CoRL 2025 exists, but the specific 2025 reviewer guidelines, review criteria, and scoring rubric details were not included in the search results. For the most up-to-date and complete CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, you may want to visit the official OpenReview page directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference or check the CoRL website at corl.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"09510fa2-9e02-43c6-bd0b-ad3ec7ae1257","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:05:24.341Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review criteria scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017H7dwu4Kn5YVL8wSahr7Pj","content":[{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Demos | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/grou