{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012uq7hJq2zzeJfJ2nZACTDP","type":"tool_result","content":"# CORL 2025 Review Statistics\n\n**Acceptance Rate:**\nThe data shows 221 papers accepted out of 263 total submissions, yielding an acceptance rate of 84.03%. This comprises 42 oral presentations (15.97%) and 179 poster presentations (68.06%).\n\n**Rating Scale & Score Information:**\nUnfortunately, the webpage does not provide specific details about CORL 2025's rating scale, mean scores, or median scores. The page indicates \"PagesLoading...\" where this data should appear, suggesting the detailed review metrics have not yet been populated or processed for the 2025 conference.\n\n**Review Form Structure:**\nThe available documentation mentions that reviewers provided ratings and confidence scores through OpenReview, but specific dimensions or detailed form structure for CORL 2025 are not disclosed on this page.\n\n**Comparison Context:**\nFor reference, CORL 2024 used a 1.70-4.00 scale with mean ratings of 3.01, while CORL 2023 used a 4.70-10.00 scale with mean ratings of 6.52—but these details don't apply to the 2025 iteration shown here."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"fc04199a-6541-472a-8b94-abb3e5a4ae61","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:05:56.776Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":219800,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CORL 2025 Review Statistics\n\n**Acceptance Rate:**\nThe data shows 221 papers accepted out of 263 total submissions, yielding an acceptance rate of 84.03%. This comprises 42 oral presentations (15.97%) and 179 poster presentations (68.06%).\n\n**Rating Scale & Score Information:**\nUnfortunately, the webpage does not provide specific details about CORL 2025's rating scale, mean scores, or median scores. The page indicates \"PagesLoading...\" where this data should appear, suggesting the detailed review metrics have not yet been populated or processed for the 2025 c