ainty): 66.8% → per-DOF > scalar by 6.0pp\n\n**Additional experiments**:\n- Per-perturbation breakdown (Table 4): gains on 6/7 types (camera +19.5, noise +17.8, robot-state +16.2, lighting +13.4, background +11.8, layout +5.2; language +2.1 not significant)\n- COC validation (Table 5): ρ=0.61, p=3e-5; ACI coverage 0.89 vs static 0.78; 28% volume narrowing\n- A5 (CGS vs Bonferroni): joint Mahalanobis beats Bonferroni by 3.4pp, Bonferroni 35% larger volumes\n- A6 (COC vs episode-level ACI): similar final perf (72.8 vs 72.1), COC 2.5x faster convergence, +4.2pp early\n- A7 (epistemic vs aleatoric): CGS 45D (72.8%) >> DiU 7D (63.9%), combined 52D only +0.7pp more\n- Feature importance: conformal radius 48%, std 31%, ellipsoid volume 21%; perturbation-specific top features differ\n- SnapFlow: 71.2% at 38ms (4.9x speedup), 87% diversity retained\n- MVP point-reaching: per-DOF 0.0735 < scalar 0.0788 < none 0.0882\n\n**Experiment design context** (from review_context.yaml — the full experiment plan):\nThe paper covers all 14 planned experiments. The context lists expected results that match what the paper reports. Planned tables/figures include:\n- Tables 1-8 plus S1-S5 (supplementary)\n- Figures 1-14 plus S1-S5\nHowever, the 7-page paper only shows Tables 1-8 inline; the supplementary figures/tables are referenced but appear to be in supplementary material not included in this PDF.\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed R1 review focused on **Methods** and **Experiments**. Structure your review as:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences, your own words)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on methodological soundness and experimental rigor)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on methodological gaps, experimental concerns, missing controls)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues** (presentation, notation, etc.)\n6. **Scores**: Rate each dimension 1-10:\n   - Soundness (methodological rigor)\n   - Empirical quality (experimental coverage, statistical 