{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHMYG6AnGy4hJZi8vkkRQt","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_8/projects/acr-vla-conformal-refinement/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 6\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 01:03 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 方案确定：3D Point-Reaching Motivating Experiment 验证 per-DOF conformal 特征的信息优势\\\\n  rationale: IDEA_BRIEF 已设计了完美的 go/no-go gate：用合成数据的 3D reaching task 对比 per-DOF vs\\\\n    标量 vs 无不确定性三种 conditioning，直接测试核心假设。成本极低（<0.5 GPU-hours），无需 VLA 基础设施，失败则提前止损。Pass\\\\n    标准明确：B 在非扰动轴 MSE 比 A 低 >10%。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 01:06 UTC\\\\n  summary: 采纳 Reviewer 建议完善 MVP：增加 B vs C 对比（>5% MSE）、K=10 estimated uncertainty variant、2:1/1.5:1\\\\n    各向异性 sweep\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 正确指出 (1) 缺少 B vs C 对比会遗漏\\\\\\\"观测特征已足够\\\\\\\"的可能性，这直接关系核心 claim；(2) oracle\\\\n    uncertainty 与实际 pipeline 存在 gap，K=10 variant 几乎零成本可验证；(3) 5:1 比率过极端，需测试更温和情况。三项改进均不增加显著成本。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 01:47 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP 通过，GO — 进入 research 阶段\\\\n  rationale: 全部 3 条 pass 标准满足且 margin 很大：per-DOF (B) 在非扰动轴 MSE 比标量 (A) 低 22-38%，比无\\\\n    uncertainty (C) 低 15-39%。K=10 estimated 和弱各向异性(1.5:1)下均成立。核心假设\\\\\\\"per-DOF conformal\\\\n    特征携带更多可操作信息\\\\\\\"得到验证。关注风险：oracle→K=10 衰减 ~15pp，真实 7-DOF 场景待验证。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: mvp-point-reaching\\\\n    role: MVP gate\\\\n    result: PASS — all 6 conditions met criteria\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  - D002\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 02:59 UTC\\\\n  summary: Horizon 策略：截取 chunk 前 H_eff=5 步，action_dim=6。CGS 输出 40D。\\\\n  rationale: SmolVLA chunk_size=50 远超原假设 H=5。receding-horizon 执行语义下只需关注近期 action 的\\\\n    uncertainty，远期 step 对当前校正无意义。H_eff=5 保持与 IDEA_BRIEF 设计一致，CGS 40D 可控（per-DOF std\\\\n    30 + radius 5 + volume 5），p/n=6/10=0.6 优于原假设 0.7。H_eff=10 留作 ablation。action_dim=6\\\\n    使 Ledoit-Wolf 更稳定。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-13 03:00 UTC\\\\n  summary: 不等 Dream 重新提交，直接启动 P0 实验。Dream zombie 占槽，Reviewer 已两轮审核通过 framing/plan。\\\\n  rationale: Dream dream_20260513T015051 崩溃在 review 阶段（imagine+write 已完成），zombie 状态占用并发槽位无法重新提交。但\\\\n    Reviewer 已独立完成两轮审核：(1) MVP pass 标准完善通过，(2) ROADMAP/framing/plan 审查通过。framing 和\\\\n    plan 无结构性缺陷。GPU 空闲不应再等——继续阻塞的唯一收益是 Dream 的模拟审稿反馈，但 Reviewer 已覆盖了主要风险点。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D003\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2106, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9MWD8xUBVCyK2j19WEhKH","session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"ce2a59b8-00d5-4feb-a996-2e533e37dca0","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:07:04.235Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WXkmEQjZ3No5h3bh1Yu1Nr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P9iGyaoJNMsagJandJ7kiD","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"acr-vla-conformal-refinement","file":"paper_checklist.yaml","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3262,"cache_read_input_tokens":17902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9MWD8xUBVCyK2j19WEhKH","session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"c740d302-f7de-41f3-8e88-36debe835936"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P9iGyaoJNMsagJandJ7kiD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": false, \\\"data\\\": {}, \\\"error\\\": \\\"No paper_checklist.yaml found for 'acr-vla-conformal-refinement'.\\\", \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9MWD8xUBVCyK2j19WEhKH","session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"e2ca66c5-b040-42c5-ab55-948dbfddea9b","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:07:04.915Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Bx2iTuMz59ACWipTGDoBdS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SF4MGWJMnDiiipbE2UyZTq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **Novelty** and **Related Work**.\n\n## Venue: CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning)\n- Evaluation dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n- Rating scale: 1-10 (10=top 5% seminal, 8=clear accept, 6=marginally above threshold, 5=marginally below)\n- Acceptance rate historically ~25-35%\n- CoRL values: robotics relevance, empirical rigor, real-world applicability, honest limitations\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: ACR-VLA: Inference-Time Dimension-Selective Action Correction via Multivariate Conformal Prediction for Vision-Language-Action Models\n\n**Core idea**: An inference-time module for flow-matching VLAs that extracts per-DOF conformal statistics from K=10 samples (CGS: 45D features with Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage) and feeds them into a lightweight CRM (131K params, ~12ms overhead) for dimension-selective action correction. Uses Adaptive Conformal Inference (ACI) driven by a novel Chunk Overlap Consistency (COC) signal.\n\n**Three claims**:\n1. Per-DOF conformal features enable dimension-selective correction (12pp ablation gap)\n2. COC as self-referential ACI signal (ρ=0.61, 2.5x faster convergence vs episode-level)\n3. Orthogonal to training-time methods (ACR-VLA+SRPO = 88.7% new SOTA)\n\n**Related work discussed in paper**:\n- Robustness of VLA models: LIBERO-Plus, SRPO (82.1% SOTA), RobustVLA, DiG-Flow, ReconVLA, SAFE\n- Conformal prediction in robotics: CP-in-the-Loop, UPS, safe set construction → all treat CP as binary decision, ACR-VLA uses as continuous features\n- Uncertainty quantification: DiU (aleatoric, single pass), A2C2 (generic residual) → neither provides calibrated per-DOF epistemic features\n\n**Method components**:\n- CGS: 45D features from K=10 samples with Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage, Mahalanobis nonconformity score\n- ACI+COC: Novel COC signal for online conformal threshold adaptation without external supervision\n- CRM: 131K param MLP, residual correction conditioned on CGS features\n\n**Key experiment results**:\n- +15pp on base SmolVLA (LIBERO-Plus), -0.8pp nominal\n- +6.6pp stacked on SRPO → 88.7% new SOTA\n- A3 ablation: 12pp gap confirms conformal features are primary driver\n- A4: per-DOF > scalar by 6pp\n- A7: CGS epistemic (72.8%) >> DiU aleatoric (63.9%)\n- A6: COC vs episode-level: similar final perf, COC 2.5x faster convergence\n- Per-perturbation: gains on 6/7 types, language not significant (honest limitation)\n- SnapFlow integration: 4.9x speedup, -1.6pp\n\n**References**: Only 5 references cited [1]-[5]: LIBERO, LIBERO-Plus, SRPO, ReconVLA, SAFE\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed R2 review focused on **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Structure your review as:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences, your own words)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on novelty of contributions, positioning vs prior art)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on novelty concerns, missing related work, overclaiming)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Rate each dimension 1-10:\n   - Originality\n   - Related work coverage\n   - Clarity\n   - Significance\n   - Overall recommendation\n   - Confidence (1-5, 5=expert)\n\nBe particularly critical about:\n- Whether the novelty claims are justified given prior work in conformal prediction, residual policies, and uncertainty-conditioned correction\n- The reference list has ONLY 5 entries — assess whether this is adequate for a top venue\n- Whether \"first to combine multivariate CP with learned residual correction\" is truly novel or an incremental combination\n- Whether COC is genuinely novel or a repackaging of temporal consistency checking\n- Whether the framing of \"orthogonal gains\" is overclaiming — what would falsify this?\n- Missing comparisons: A2C2, CP-in-the-Loop, DiU, RobustVLA, DiG-Flow are mentioned but not experimentally compared\n- The paper only evaluates on one base VLA (SmolVLA) and one benchmark suite (LIBERO/LIBERO-Plus)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":56985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":406},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c62bef3-f4e7-4ad6-8c63-7057bfddfd08","uuid":"f4db3d52-010e-4807-ad7e-fde04e115fee"}
